#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/lib/qtwebengine.xml:25
#, xml-text
msgid "Introduction to QtWebEngine"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/lib/qtwebengine.xml:31
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<application>QtWebEngine</application> integrates "
"<application>chromium</application>'s web capabilities into Qt. It ships "
"with its own copy of ninja which it uses for the build if it cannot find a "
"system copy, and various copies of libraries from ffmpeg, icu, libvpx, and "
"zlib (including libminizip) which have been forked by the "
"<application>chromium</application> developers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/lib/qtwebengine.xml:40
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This package and browsers using it may be useful if you need to use a "
"website designed for google chrome, or chromium, browsers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><warning><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/lib/qtwebengine.xml:46
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"QtWebEngine uses a forked copy of chromium, and is therefore vulnerable to "
"many issues found there. The Qt developers seem to fork a newer version for "
"minor Qt versions, but because chromium moves to newer versions very often, "
"by the time the Qt developers get a forked version to pass their extended "
"tests it is always an old version and security fixes from chromium (some of "
"which have a CVE number) can take several months to appear in a QtWebengine "
"release, even if the severity has been rated as Critical."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><warning><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/lib/qtwebengine.xml:57
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Therefore, you should be wary of using QtWebEngine in a sensitive context "
"and should always update to the next release as soon as it appears in this "
"book, even if is not flagged as a Security Update.  Identifying which "
"vulnerabilities have been fixed in a particular release requires pulling the"
" appropriate 'based-NNN' branch just before the previous and current "
"releases and is often impractical. Reports of fixed QTBUG items do not seem "
"to be available and there is not any documentation in the tarball for "
"changes after the qt-5 versions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><warning><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/lib/qtwebengine.xml:72
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"By default, ninja will use all online CPUs +2 (if at least 4 exist), even if"
" they are not available to the current task because the build terminal has "
"been restricted with 'taskset'.  In BLFS, this package takes more time to "
"build than any other.  In one example, the build of this package crashed at "
"about the 90 percent point due to an out of memory problem on a system with "
"24 cores and 32 GB of memory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><warning><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/lib/qtwebengine.xml:82
#, xml-text
msgid "To work around this, see the Command Explanations below."
msgstr ""

